    "source": "school_textbook",
    "content": "함수 $f(x)=3x^{2}-6x+2$에 대하여\n$\\lim _{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(a+h)-f(a-h)}{h}=6$\n을 만족시키는 $a$의 값을 구하시오.",
    "answer": "$\\frac{3}{2}$",
    "solution": "$\\lim _{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(a+h)-f(a-h)}{h}$\n$=\\lim _{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)+f(a)-f(a-h)}{h}$\n$=\\lim _{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h}+\\lim _{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(a-h)-f(a)}{-h}$\n$=f\\,'(a)+f\\,'(a)=2f\\,'(a)=6$이므로 $f\\,'(a)=3$\n$f\\,'(x)=(3x^{2}-6x+2)'=6x-6$이므로\n$f\\,'(a)=6a-6=3$에서 $a=\\frac{3}{2}$",
